{:edb/db-before-t 1280 :edb/db-after-t 1281 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534593 50 #inst "2026-10-08T01:52:30.650Z" 13194139534593 true] [17592186083136 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297694 13194139534593 true] [17592186083137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297673 13194139534593 true] [17592186083137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297687 13194139534593 true] [17592186083138 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297680 13194139534593 true] [17592186083138 1020 #edb/ref 17592186297701 13194139534593 true] [17592186297673 1017 #edb/ref 17592186297674 13194139534593 true] [17592186297673 1089 "q-122479" 13194139534593 true] [17592186297673 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534593 true] [17592186297673 1100 "Erik has an encyclopedia with $24$ tomes and is selecting $3$ tomes to read first, second, and third. How many different choices does Erik have?" 13194139534593 true] [17592186297673 1113 #uuid "a016216d-8f23-59da-bb6c-067b39c3dc00" 13194139534593 true] [17592186297673 1145 "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $24$ tomes to choose from, so $n=24.$ We want to select $3$ of those tomes for Erik to read, so we have $r=3.$\n\nTherefore, the number of choices Erik has is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{24}{P}_{3} & =\\frac{24!}{(24-3)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{24!}{21!} \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\cdot 23\\cdot 22\\cdot \\cancel{21!}}{\\cancel{21!}} \\\\  & =24\\cdot 23\\cdot 22 \\\\  & =12\\,144.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534593 true] [17592186297674 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297675 13194139534593 true] [17592186297674 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297676 13194139534593 true] [17592186297674 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297677 13194139534593 true] [17592186297674 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297678 13194139534593 true] [17592186297674 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297679 13194139534593 true] [17592186297674 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534593 true] [17592186297674 1041 "selection" 13194139534593 true] [17592186297674 1104 #edb/ref 17592186297676 13194139